    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nOn gfx950, the sparse MLA indexer's prefill path gathers the FP8 K cache with AITER's `cp_gather_indexer_k_quant_cache` instead of the Triton kernel. This is the prefill-gather part of #46172 (tjtanaa), rebased on current main. Draft until the measurements below are in.\n\n## Claims\n\n- GLM-5.2 / GLM-5.3 / DeepSeek-V3.2 prefill on MI355X uses AITER's gather kernel, which should lower TTFT on long prompts.\n- Decode is unchanged, and so is the DeepSeek-V4 C4A block-flat case.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Check | Status |\n|---|---|\n| GLM-5.3 TP4 MI355X, GPQA and RULER NIAH, on vs off | pending |\n| TTFT on long-prompt prefill, on vs off (TPOT should not move) | pending |\n| Trace: `_cp_gather_indexer_quant_cache_gfx950_kernel` replaced by the AITER kernel | pending |\n\n## Details\n\n- AITER's op takes the layout as one flag, `preshuffle`. `preshuffle = kv_cache.shape[1] > 1` is the Triton wrapper's default (`NORMAL` when `block_size == 1`, else `SHUFFLE`).\n- AITER cannot express the explicit `cache_layout=\"NORMAL\"` override that DeepSeek-V4 C4A (`compress_ratio == 4`) needs, so that case stays on Triton.\n- AITER derives the token-to-sequence map from `cu_seq_lens`, so `token_to_seq` is not passed.\n- Gated on `_ON_GFX950`.\n\n**Relation to #46172.** The rest of #46172 is on main, superseded, or skipped for these models:\n\n| #46172 change | Status on main |\n|---|---|\n| `FP8_DTYPE` at module level | already present |\n| `top_k_per_row_decode` to AITER | superseded by `_launch_aiter_top_k_per_row_decode` (#52882) |\n| `indexer_k_quant_and_cache_triton` to AITER | not called: `fused_norm_rope` writes the indexer K cache and the indexer is built with `skip_k_cache_insert=True` |\n| `cp_gather_indexer_k_quant_cache_triton` to AITER | this PR |\n\n#46172 has had merge conflicts since 2026-08-22. Happy to close this in favour of it if it is rebased.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
